PN,30606
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1786112310
OL,3,CScientists use AI to design new
OL,4,Cviruses never seen before in nature
OL,6,F"Although this is promising for life
OL,7,Fsciences applications, it also raises
OL,8,Furgent biosafety and biosecurity
OL,9,Fquestions," doctors from the Johns
OL,10,FHopkins Center for Health Security
OL,11,Fwrote in a corresponding article
OL,12,Fpublished in Science.
OL,14,F"The ability to compose viral genomes
OL,15,Fusing generative AI now exists; the
OL,16,Fgovernance to safely steer it does
OL,17,Fnot."
OL,26,@nD@AOUqD@KO]vD@AOUyD@EO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30607
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1786112310
OL,3,CScientists use AI to design new
OL,4,Cviruses never seen before in nature
OL,6,FThe researchers addressed the
OL,7,Fbiosecurity considerations directly in
OL,8,Ftheir research, but the Johns Hopkins
OL,9,Fdoctors wrote that they "engage with
OL,10,Fbiosafety and biosecurity questions
OL,11,Fmore deliberately than most developers
OL,12,Fof powerful biological AI models".
OL,14,FThe new research focused on E. coli
OL,15,Fbacteria and was in a certain type of
OL,16,Fvirus that can't affect humans ` and
OL,17,Fit's unclear how well the work would
OL,18,Fapply to other viruses.
OL,26,@qD@YOUtD@aO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30608
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1786112310
OL,3,CScientists use AI to design new
OL,4,Cviruses never seen before in nature
OL,6,FThe authors of the response article
OL,7,Fsingle out one particularly risky area
OL,8,Fthat they say should not be pursued:
OL,9,Feukaryote-infecting pathogens (spread
OL,10,Fby organisms with complex cells and
OL,11,Fnuclei).
OL,13,FThese can cause a variety of illness
OL,14,Fin humans including malaria an yeast
OL,15,Finfections.
OL,17,F"Such genomes might encode new
OL,18,Fpathogens that can infect humans,
OL,19,Fanimals, or plants in ways that cannot
OL,20,Fbe contained by existing
OL,21,Fcountermeasures," the authors wrote.
OL,26,@yD@AOU}D@QO]
